# Standard Input Prompt Template

Use this exact prompt every time you start a campaign. Replace the `[COMPANY]` and `[IDEA_PLACEHOLDER]` parts.

---

## Template

```
@raw-to-idea Run this through the pipeline for [COMPANY]:

[IDEA_PLACEHOLDER]
```

---

## Examples

### 1. Raw text idea
```
@raw-to-idea Run this through the pipeline for 91astrology:

A campaign about clarity vs confusion for the Nadi Report — showing how people feel lost in life decisions until they get their personalized Nadi reading.
```

### 2. Image of a real ad
```
@raw-to-idea Run this through the pipeline for 91astrology:

[upload image screenshot]

This is a competitor ad I saw on Instagram. Deconstruct it and reimagine the strategy for our Nadi Report.
```

### 3. URL to a live ad
```
@raw-to-idea Run this through the pipeline for mycompany:

https://www.example.com/landing-page

Analyze this landing page and build an ad campaign concept around their core offer, adapted for our product.
```

### 4. Idea pool reference
```
@raw-to-idea Run this through the pipeline for 91astrology:

Use idea-01 from the idea pool. I want to keep the core concept but change the platform to YouTube Shorts and language to Hindi.
```

### 5. Research-first approach
```
@raw-to-idea Run this through the pipeline for 91astrology:

I want to run a campaign about [TOPIC]. Before we build the creative, do the research phase first — I want to see what signals, competitors, and audience insights you find before we commit to a creative direction.
```

---

## What happens next

1. The raw-to-idea agent identifies the company from your prompt
2. Loads the company profile from `../company_profiles/{company}.json` (relative to OpenMontage repo root)
3. Reads your input (text, image, or URL)
4. Asks up to 3 clarifying questions
5. Locks the brief after your confirmation
6. Writes the idea to `{company_paths.idea_pool}/`
7. Initializes the campaign workspace (session, README, directories)
8. **Hands off to the main agent** to orchestrate the pipeline stages:
   - research → creative_concept → copy → assets → review
9. The main agent spawns specialized subagents per stage and presents final deliverables

You do nothing else.
